<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
This lists menu sections that a user can select when creating a new eRequest.

IMPORTANT:
It is safe to ADD new menu sections and RENAME existing descriptions in this list.

However, REMOVING menu sections is more problemactic as it could mean clients on legacy systems could raise incidents under menu sections that no longer exist in our system. (and thus will not be assigned to the correct Product Area)
To prevent this from happening, you will need to:
	1. Write a EDI specific transformation to add a new mapping to the LegacyMenuSectionMappings (EDI specific registry) which maps the removed menu section to one of the valid menu sections
	 - This will allow eRequests raised with legacy menu sections to be automatically redirected to the correct Product Area in ediProd
	
	2. Write a transformation to convert all current eRequests (IncidentApproval.IA_Module) with this legacy menu section to the new menu section.
	3. Write a EDI Specific transformation to convert all current incidents (IncidentMain.IM_Module) with this legacy menu section to the new menu section.
	
	
See Richard Smith or Andrew Luong if you require assistance.


-->
<CodeDescriptionPairList
	xmlns="http://www.edi.com.au/CodeDescriptionPairList.xsd"
	xmlns:cdpl="http://www.edi.com.au/CodeDescriptionPairList.xsd"
	cdpl:Sort="true"
	cdpl:SortType="Description"
	cdpl:Localizable="true">
	
	<BaseClass Name="CustomerServiceMenuSection.Lookup"/>
	<Namespace Name="Enterprise.ZArchitecture.Modules"/>
	
